{
  "duration": 70.839,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.119,
      "end": 0.259,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.719,
      "end": 1.539,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.259,
      "end": 3.399,
      "text": "It's time to solve"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.079,
      "end": 5.039,
      "text": "one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.639,
      "end": 6.46,
      "text": "Now in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.059,
      "end": 7.899,
      "text": "we are given that"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.42,
      "end": 10.019,
      "text": "the length of the train is"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.619,
      "end": 11.799,
      "text": "two hundred fifty meters."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.199,
      "end": 14.639,
      "text": "The length of the platform is three hundred fifty meters,"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.279,
      "end": 16.399,
      "text": "and the speed of the train"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.94,
      "end": 18.76,
      "text": "is seventy-two kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.279,
      "end": 24.579,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find how much time the train will take to completely cross the platform."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.059,
      "end": 26.34,
      "text": "Now the important point here is"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.68,
      "end": 28.439,
      "text": "completely cross the platform."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.859,
      "end": 29.699,
      "text": "What does this mean?"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.279,
      "end": 33.88,
      "text": "It means the train has to cover its own length as well as the platform length."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.38,
      "end": 37.72,
      "text": "So the total distance will be two hundred fifty plus three hundred fifty,"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.2,
      "end": 39.459,
      "text": "which is six hundred meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.079,
      "end": 41.279,
      "text": "Now that we have the distance,"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.619,
      "end": 44.239,
      "text": "we only need the speed in meters per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.719,
      "end": 47.839,
      "text": "We know that seventy-two multiplied by five upon eighteen"
    },
    {
      "start": 48.34,
      "end": 52.599,
      "text": "gives us twenty meters per second. Done. Now we have both the values we need."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.099,
      "end": 55.539,
      "text": "Time is equal to distance divided by speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.959,
      "end": 63.419,
      "text": "Putting the values in the formula, we get six hundred divided by twenty. After solving this, the time comes out to be thirty seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.279,
      "end": 70.839,
      "text": "So the final answer will be thirty seconds. Hence, the correct option is option B."
    }
  ],
